<FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">price-to-book</FONT></FONT> approaches and placed lesser emphasis on the <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">price-to-assets</FONT></FONT> approach in estimating pro&nbsp;forma market value. The peer group consisted of ten publicly traded, fully converted thrifts or thrift holding companies based in the <FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">Mid-Atlantic</FONT> regions of the United States with assets between $7.0&nbsp;billion and $25.0&nbsp;billion. The peer group included companies with: </P>
