<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">At December&nbsp;31, 2025 and 2024, the allowance for credit losses related to PCD loans was $2.6&nbsp;million and $2.9&nbsp;million,
respectively. Loans <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">held-for-sale,</FONT></FONT> when applicable, are excluded from the allowance for credit losses coverage ratios in the table above. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B><I>Allocation of Allowance for Credit Losses</I></B><B>.</B> The following table sets forth the allowance for credit losses allocated by
loan category and the percent of loans in each category to total loans at the dates indicated. The allowance for credit losses allocated to each category is not necessarily indicative of future losses in any particular category and does not restrict
the use of the allowance to absorb losses in other categories. </P> <P STYLE="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
