respectively, for which no provision for income tax has been made. This amount represents an allocation of income to bad debt deductions for tax purposes only. Events that would result in taxation of these reserves include the failure to qualify as
a bank for tax purposes, distributions in complete or partial liquidation, stock redemptions and excess distributions to stockholders. </P>
